          <p>The <code>opm</code> subcommands, flags, and functionality related to the SQLite database format are also deprecated and will be removed in a future release. The features are still supported and must be used for catalogs that use the deprecated SQLite database format.</p>
          <p>Many of the <code>opm</code> subcommands and flags for working with the SQLite database format, such as <code>opm index prune</code>, do not work with the file-based catalog format. For more information about working with file-based catalogs, see "Operator Framework packaging format", "Managing custom catalogs", and "Mirroring images for a disconnected installation by using the oc-mirror plugin v2".</p>
